    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The Ozark region of the United States midcontinent is host for the largest Mississippi Valley-type (MVT) lead-zinc province in the world. The region includes the world-class districts of the Old Lead Belt, Viburnum Trend, and Tri-State districts and the smaller Northern Arkansas, Central Missouri, and Southeast Missouri barite districts. This report provides a list of references for a wide variety of topics on the ores that includes the geology, geochemistry, and environmental studies. The organization of the report is alphabetical by author, then by the year of publication and lastly alphabetical by title.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
